(a) whether Government is considering a proposal to roll out petrol blended with 25 per cent ethanol;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether it is a fact that there is already growing concern over the impact of E20 petrol on vehicle mileage and performance; and
(d) if so, the details and Government’s reaction thereto?

(a) whether Vizhinjam international port -rail connectivity project, of which land acquisition is already completed, has been included in the PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan;
(b) whether the Ministry will consider to undertake the construction of the 10.7 kms new line connectivity from Vizhinjam port to the main railway line of Thiruvananthapuram (TVM) division to generate a  steady revenue utilizing the Vizhinjam Port; and
(c) whether the Ministry on completion of the project would be willing to undertake operation and maintenance of the above new Railway line though it started as a State project?

(a) whether it is a fact that the NITI Aayog has made a slew of recommendations on regulation, research, trade, education and diplomacy to transform Ayurveda as an integral component of global health care system by 2047;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the steps being taken to achieve the target on time?

(a) whether it is a fat that the price of Brent Crude has dropped nearly 44 per cent from $126.41 a barrel om April 30 to about $70.78 on July 2, 2026;
(b) if so, the details there of; and
(c) the decision taken by Government about reducing the prices of petrol and petroleum products including LPG proportionately?

(a) whether it is a fact that the VB-G RAM-G Scheme introduced in place of MGNREGA has come into force w.e.f. 1st, July  2026;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government’s attention has been drawn to the protests by various organisations against the replacement of MGNREGA by a new scheme;
(d) if so, the details of the concerns expressed by these organisations against the new scheme and demanding the restoration of the old scheme; and
(e) Government’s response thereto?

(a) whether Government has announced Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) with European Union (EU) in January, 2026 which has been termed as 'Mother of All Deals';
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of sectors/industries likely to be benefitted by this agreement with EU; and 
(d) if so, the salient features of the agreement and its impact on future trade with EU countries?

(a) whether the Sixteenth Finance Commission and the latest Public Enterprises Survey have reported some 383 Government run inoperative firms across the country for decades, but not officially shut down;
(b) whether earlier Finance Commissions had also mentioned about the inactive  Public Sector Undertakings owned by State or Centre and had recommended for immediate closure to reduce fiscal strain; and
(c) if so, the State-wise details of such PSUs and Government’s decision on the same?

(a) whether it is a fact that the sales and imports of various fertilizers have surged in April-January 2025-26 while Government was aiming to cut urea and diammonium phospate (DAP) consumption by introducing nano variants of the fertilizers;
(b) if so, the details of the domestic production of Urea and DAP during the year 2025-26 so far and the import and total sale of these fertilizers during the same period; and
(c) the reasons for the surge in the consumption of fertilizers during the same period?

(a) in view of the announcement made by the Expenditure Secretary in the Finance Ministry that the key focus of Government’s ?12.2 lakh crore Capex for the next financial year will be mainly on sectors like ship building, national high ways, railways and the urban sector to the extent of metro train projects, whether Government will consider the proposal of the Kerala Government for a Rapid Rail (RRTS) project from Trivandrum to Kasaragod;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the other sectors in Kerala which can be considered for the financial assistance from this fund?

(a) whether it is a fact that the UGC has put in the public domain, a draft guidelines on Uniform policy on Mental Health and Well-Being for Higher Educational Institutions (HEIs) for stake holders feed back;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether it is a fact that the UGC draft offers guidance and training support, but has no earmarked grants or implementation timelines, placing the entire operational and financial burden on HEIs that most of the Universities and Colleges cannot afford due to their financial crunch; and
(d) if so, the details and Government’s reaction thereto?

(a) whether it is a fact that the production of wheat and rice has increased recently and Government is facing surplus situation;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the increase in production is due to the improved productivity or the increased area of cultivation of the food grains, the details thereof; and
(d) whether it is a fact that the incentive bonus being given to the farmers to increase the production has been stopped by Central Government and States have been asked to discourage farmers to produce food grains?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is a recent trend of road contractors quoting low bids of up to 48 per cent less than the estimated project cost largely due to aggressive bidding which usually has a direct bearing on the quality of work;
(b) whether it is a fact that a number of complaints about the collapse of National Highways and flyovers under construction, particularly in Kerala have been reported recently; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and action taken against the contractors in these cases?

(a) whether Government is facing the prospect of large surplus of Wheat and Rice stocks and it has reflected in the declining prices of these commodities;
(b) if so, the details of the Wheat and Rice buffer stocks with the FCI; and
(c) whether the surplus situation is because of the increase in the supply side and decreasing demand, the details thereof?

(a) whether construction workers are eligible for maternity-care, pension, housing, health-care, education and daily commute on Government buses and only 1 to 10 per cent receive these benefits in Delhi;
(b) if so, the details of welfare schemes offered to construction workers registered in Delhi under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Act;
(c) the number of workers registered under the Act and those availing the benefits; and
(d) the measures proposed to be taken to educate the workers about their benefits so that the purpose of the Act is better served?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has decided to reduce the cut off for NEET PG 2025 to zero percentage level on the ground that thousands of seats in medical colleges lying vacant;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of vacant seats in Government medical colleges and private medical colleges separately;
d) whether it is a fact that majority of seats are vacant in private medical colleges where the fees run into crores which most candidates cannot afford; and
(e) if so, the details thereof and Government’s reaction thereto?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government had given certain dispensation/variations to the airlines on pilots duty and rest period norms;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether these relief on pilot’s duty norms has been withdrawn, so that safety is not compromised, if not, the reasons therefor; and 
(d) the steps being taken for a periodic review of the recruitment of pilots by airlines by the aviation safety regulator, DGCA?

V

(a) whether it is a fact that the funds allocated for Pradhan Mantri Gramin Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) have been grossly underutilized for the last two years and for the current financial year, the utilization is very meagre;
(b) if so, the details of the funds allocated during the year 2024, 2025 and 2026 and the actual utilization during these years; and
(c) the reasons for under-utilization and remedial measures proposed to be taken to see that such Centrally Sponsored Schemes (CSS) are properly implemented by the States?

(a) whether the Ministry offers any plan for redevelopment of tourist sites affected by natural disasters, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry has conducted any study of tourist places that are geologically sensitive or prone to natural disasters and the steps taken to promote tourism in an environmentally sustainable manner;
(c) whether the Ministry, in coordination with the State Governments, regulates tourism in ecologically sensitive zones and if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(d) the details of deaths or injuries caused to tourists due to natural disasters during the last five years?

(a) details of existing toll collection booths on National Highways, including the process of allocation from Government agencies to private entities;
(b) details of toll collected by private entities in the last five years, State-wise, year-wise details for the last five years;
(c) how many toll booths on National Highways were found to be collecting toll in violation of existing rules in the last five years;
(d) details of action taken against violators for collecting toll in excess of the amount permissible under rules; and
(e) the details of penalties collected from commuters for not using FASTag, State-wise?

(a) whether the Ministry has estimated the post-harvest food losses in India for perishables and grains, if so, details of volume, category and value wise data of post-harvest food loss for the last year;
(b) data of State-wise availability of cold storages and cold-chains, including capacity and its utilisation by different crops;
(c) whether the Ministry has any estimate of the impact of food loss on food prices and green house gas emissions; and
(d) whether the Ministry has identified the need to establish cold-storages in the Southern part of the country, considering high temperatures and humidity, if so, details of progress made?

(a) the schemes for education being implemented in States by the Ministry, details of budgetary outlay, including Union and States’ contribution to each scheme;
(b) whether there are schemes being run by the Ministry that are contingent upon implementing the NEP, 2020, if so, the specific schemes thereof; and
(c) the list of funds pending under the various schemes by the Ministry, State-wise?

(a) the extent and quantum of the recently undertaken GST reforms;
(b) whether the Ministry has undertaken any study of the reforms’ effects on the economy, the exchequer and the common people;
(c) the category-wise annual data of GST collection for the last five years; and
(d) the head-wise difference in the total amount of GST collected under old and new GST rates in the last five years?

(a) the data of airline operators flouting the safety standards set by the DGCA, the AAI or the BCAS during the last five years, including details of the nature of violation and the action taken, yearly and airline-wise;
(b) the budget outlay for safety and enforcement of regulations during the last five years; and
(c) current status of vacancies against sanctioned posts in the DGCA, the AAI, the BCAS and Air Traffic Controllers?

(a) the amount and percent of total budget outlay earmarked for mental health out of the budget estimates for the current financial year for the Ministry;
(b) the channels for the Ministry to utilise the amount allocated to mental health, and details of the data of allocations for different programmes for the last five years;
(c) the budgetary allocation for mental health under the Tertiary Care Programme (TCP), since 2021–22; and
(d) whether the Ministry has identified reasons for under-utilisation of funds for the Tele MANAS programme?

(a) specify the process of allocating coal mines since the introduction of Coal Mines (Special Provisions) Act, 2025 and the differences it brought compared to earlier process;
(b) enlist the mines allocated under the Act, since its commencement and whether Government has done any study of its benefits compared to the earlier policy;
(c) whether any environment relaxations have been provided for coal mining since the introduction of the Act; and
(d) number of trees felled to clear coal mines allocated under the Act, State-wise?

(a) the details of notified substances under the NDPS Act seized by the agencies under the Ministry like the DRI and Customs Department on Indian ports during last five years, year-wise and instance-wise details including port, drug seized, quantity and estimated values;
(b) the details of notified substances under the NDPS Act that were seized during attempts to import or export the drugs, year-wise and port-wise; and 
(c) details of action taken against the importers and exporters of the drugs, FIRs filed, charge sheets accepted and firms or individuals convicted for importing or exporting notified drugs?

(a) the existing criteria for determining poverty for a household in rural and urban areas, details of headcount for poor according to existing criteria;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any survey to asses the level of poverty during the last three years;
(c) whether Government intends to update the criteria for determining poverty line in tune with climate change and erratic weather impacting livelihoods; and
(d) number of people lifted from poverty according to Government data during the last three years, including the basis or study conducted to determine the number, nature and extent taken into consideration to define poverty?

(a) the status of current Maternal Mortality Ratio (MMR) and Infant Mortality Rate (IMR) across the country & States and details of the State-wise progress made in the last five years, including the source of data furnished;
(b) the number and details of States that have achieved the UN targets in reducing MMR and IMR, and details of any incentives Union Government is providing to such States;
(c) the special steps being taken by the Ministry to focus on States that are yet to reach the UN determined targets of MMR and IMR; and
(d) the amount spent by the Ministry in combating maternal mortality and infant mortality, State-wise?

(a) number of petitions received by National Commission for Minorities (NCM) since 2019, year-wise, community-wise data of petitions received and disposed during this time period;
(b) number of FIRs lodged after intervention by NCM, provide year-wise, community-wise data of FIRs lodged and action taken thereon;
(c) whether NCM has taken note of instances of hate speech in public forums against minorities steps  NCM is taking to curb hate speech; and
(d) whether Government has taken note of the vacancy of Christian member in the NCM, the steps taken to fill vacancy in the NCM?

(a) the number of new hostel seats built, seats increased under the scheme during last five years, year-wise, for State/UT/University for boys and girls;
(b) yearly expenditure incurred under the scheme for building hostels and details of funds allocated to State/UT/University, year-wise; and
(c) the number of hostels for which the last grant of 5 per cent was released post occupation of hostel rooms by OBC boys and girls, rooms occupied by students, year-wise?

(a) State-wise data of students eligible for pre-matric, post matric and merit cum means scholarship under the Ministry; 
(b) State-wise data of students eligible for the scholarship, students who received the above three scholarships and the amount disbursed; and 
(c) whether the Ministry is considering to extend the scope of such scholarships available to students from the minority communities?

(a) current status of CPSEs under the Ministry including turn-over and profits made in the last three years;
(b) details of CPSEs under the Ministry that have been privatised or liquified since 2019, the proceeds made from such transactions including the existing financial status of privatised or liquified entities;
(c) entity-wise number of workers affected due to privatisation or entity being liquified, details of the provisions made by the Ministry for them; and
(d) whether there are any proposals under consideration to privatise or liquify any CPSE under the Ministry, the details including the number of workers poised to be affected by such a move?

(a) number of persons booked under the Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (UAPA) State-wise during the last five years;
(b) number of persons against whom chargesheets have been filed, State-wise;
(c) number of persons convicted under the UAPA, State-wise, during the last five years;
(d) number of persons who were booked under the UAPA but charges were quashed by the judiciary; and
(e) number of persons currently booked under the UAPA and State-wise data of prisoners under the Act?

(a) the lists and number of new airports built after the commencement of the UDAN scheme and the expenditure incurred for building new, greenfield airports;
(b) the number of flights available from the newly built airports, airport-wise;
(c) the estimated capacity addition through new greenfield airports in terms of passengers and freight volume; and
(d) the passenger count for newly built airports during the last three years?

(a) the number of instances of bank failures in the last three years, including Cooperative Banks, Small Finance Banks (SFBs) and NBFCs;
(b) the number of instances where RBI imposed operational restrictions on such failed banking and non-banking financial institutions;
(c) the amount of deposits and advances in the institutions that failed to honour their commitments to borrowers and lenders in the last three years, bank-wise details of the action taken by RBI or the Ministry; and
(d) the number of depositors who received deposit insurance from Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation (DICGC),bank-wise details thereof along with the amount?

(a) the number of AIIMS in the country, including the year of sanctions and commencement of medical operations;
(b) the sanctioned strength of faculty and students in each AIIMS, the details thereof, category-wise;
(c) the number of faculty and students currently registered in each AIIMS institute, category-wise;
(d) the amount sanctioned and the amount utilised for building new institutes or upgrading older ones for each institute in the last five years; 
(e) the criteria to declare new AIIMS hospitals or upgrade existing hospitals into AIIMS; and 
(f) whether the proposal to establish new AIIMS in Kerala was taken into consideration?

(a) the details of achievements under the DAY-NULM across the seven sub-categories under the scheme during the last three years, State-wise;
(b) the details of fund allocation from the Central Government under the scheme for the last three years, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has instated awards for top performing States under the scheme, details of award-winning States for the last five years across categories; and
(d) the index that is used to identify urban poor under the scheme?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken note of exponential increases in visa fee/immigration fee by certain countries affecting Indians across visa categories;
(b) whether the Ministry maintains data on such hikes;
(c) the number of countries that have increased visa fee/immigration fee for Indians, especially for student and workers category visas in the last three years; 
(d) whether the Ministry has considered approaching such countries where visa fee hike is becoming debarring for Indians; and
(e) whether the Ministry is considering any proposal to aid Indian students and workers abroad by paying a share of the fee?

(a) the number of Vande Bharat trains operational in the country, zone-wise;
(b) the benefits the Ministry has noted in increasing the number and frequency of Vande Bharat trains;
(c) the number of trains that were rescheduled to make space for Vande Bharat trains, the details thereof, train-category wise, zone-wise; and 
(d) the number of passengers that availed the Vande Bharat trains, and the number of Vande Bharat trains running at full passenger capacity currently, zone-wise?

(a) whether the Ministry has received complains about workers working for more than legally permissible working hours in the private sector, details of the existing laws, instances of violation and the action taken by the Ministry;
(b) whether the Ministry has studied the effects of long working hours on the physical and mental health of workers; 
(c) whether the Ministry has any guideline for workers' physical and mental health in the private sector; and
(d) whether the Ministry has taken consideration of increased stress among workers, leading to extreme steps like suicides and death due to overwork, if so, details thereof?


T

(a) whether the Ministry maintains data on visa fees being collected by foreign countries from Indian citizens, country-wise data of visa fees collected in the last three years;
(b) the number of visa applications by Indian citizens being rejected in the last three years, visa-category wise and country-wise;
(c) whether the Ministry has data on the rejection of visa requests after payment of visa fee, country-wise visa fee paid by Indian citizens and applications being rejected in the last three years; and
(d) the main reasons for rejection of visa requests?

J

(a) the targets set for the PM-KUSUM scheme at the time of launch including the number of diesel pumps to be replaced, the power generation capacity to be installed both grid-connected and off-grid pumps and the targets and their execution for electricity purchase from farmers, State-wise data;
(b) the State-wise data of functioning power purchase agreements signed and the State-wise average cost of purchase of electricity from farmers, the details thereof separately for owned and leased lands; and
(c) State-wise details of credit provided for the scheme to farmers separately for public sector and private sector banks?

(a) the number of units built and amount released from the Ministry to the States under the PMAY-(U) scheme, State-wise details thereof;
(b) the category-wise data of units built/enhanced under the components of Affordable Housing in Partnership (AHP), In-Situ Slum Redevelopment (ISSR), Credit-Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS) and Beneficiary Led Construction/Enhancement (BLC);
(c) whether Government has data on the number of units sanctioned under the BLC component for enhancement of the existing dwelling unit, if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(d) the details of credit provided for the scheme by public sector and private sector banks State-wise?

(a) the number of Vande Bharat trains operational in the country, the details thereof, zone-wise;
(b) the benefits noted by Government in increasing the number and frequency of Vande Bharat trains, the details thereof, category wise, zone-wise; and
(c) the number of passengers who travelled in Vande Bharat trains and the number of Vande Bharat trains which are running at full passenger capacity currently and the average difference in fare between Vande Bharat trains and existing Express trains, the details thereof, zone-wise?

(a) the criteria defined by the Ministry for granting Institute of Eminence (IoE) status for educational institutes;
(b) the benefits that come with the IoE status in terms of funding and flexibility in determining syllabus;
(c) whether the IoEs status is linked with performance of the institute in the National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC) framework; and
(d) the current list of IoEs along with the additional benefits granted to them in terms of funding?

J

(a) the data on meat exports from India in both volume and value terms during the last three years, category-wise, year-wise;
(b) the data for sourcing of meat for exports, category-wise, State-wise;
(c) the list of top 20 exporters of meat in terms of volume;
(d) the steps taken by Government to boost meat exports from India in the last three years; and
(e) whether Government has taken note of cow-vigilantism or certain State legislations harming the meat export sector in India, if so, in what manner does Government intend to tackle the issues?

(a) the details of major and minor train accidents, collisions and derailments including the number of dead and injured persons, including railway personnel, since 2021-22 till date, zone-wise;
(b) the details of compensation provided to the victims of such accidents, including railway personnel;
(c) the progress of the installation of Kavach anti-collision system on railway tracks, expenditure incurred and system operationalised;
(d) target set by Government for 100 per cent coverage under Kavach; and
(e) whether Government has considered anti-collision and safety systems other than Kavach, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of empanelled insurance companies under Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) including criteria for empanelment, separately for public sector and private sector insurance companies, State-wise;
(b) the data on premium collected, contributions from the Central and State Governments and insurance amount paid to farmers in the last three years, State-wise;
(c) the details of complaints of irregularities, frauds and corruption in the implementation of the scheme received in the last three years and the details of action taken; and
(d) the details of action taken against insurance companies including debarment from the scheme since 2020?

(a) the number of resolutions concerning Palestine that came up for consideration in the United Nations (UN) and related bodies since the beginning of Israel-Hamas conflict;
(b) the details of the position India took on each of such resolutions in the UN and other UN related bodies;
(c) the details of the aid India has sent to Palestine during the period directly and through UN and other related bodies, yearly data since 2021; and
(d) whether India is considering any proposal to shape global opinion to affect a ceasefire in Palestine?

(a) the recommendations made by the Wildlife Institute of India (WII) in its Biodiversity Assessment Report regarding mining in the Parsa East Kete Basan (PEKB) in the Hasdeo forest region of Chattisgarh;
(b) whether the WII cautioned about the potential for Human-Animal conflict in the region due to expansion of mining activities and whether Government has identified regions where such conflicts exist;
(c) the reasons for the mining clearance granted in the region despite environmental concerns; and
(d) the number of trees to be felled to facilitate mining in the Hasdeo region?

(a) whether Government keeps data for call-drop for both private and government telecom operators, service provider-wise, for the last one year;
(b) whether Government maintains data on strength of mobile networks provided by service providers, if so, service provider-wise data for all telecom zones;
(c) whether Government imposes any penalty on service providers for call-drop or low network connectivity, if so, the criteria and details for the last one year; and
(d) the mechanisms available to consumers to report call-drops or low network connectivity, the details of the complains received and action taken in the last one year?

(a) the present status of the Pradhan Mantra Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) including the total number of yearly candidates registered, trained and given certificates under the scheme during last five years, State-wise details thereof;
(b) number of candidates who received placement assistance by Training Partners, year-wise, State-wise;
(c) number of candidates who received employment after completing training under the scheme, sector-wise, year-wise, state-wise; and
(d) the total yearly expenditure incurred under the scheme, provide both Centrally-Sponsored Centrally-Managed and Centrally-Sponsored State-Managed data?

(a) the details of the follow-up action regarding the Ministry’s decision to set up Model Degree Colleges in the Educationally Backward Districts (EBD) in the country, State-wise and districts-wise;
(b) the current status of Model Degree Colleges in EBDs, State-wise details thereof;
(c) the expenditure incurred for setting up Model Degree Colleges, State-wise; and
(d) the number of functioning Model Degree Colleges after the identification of EBDs, State-wise details?

(a) details of the conception of the Namami Gange Project and details of the work done under the project, expenditure incurred on  various active and completed projects;
(b) the estimated sewage generated by towns along the Ganga river, the difference in sewage quantity reaching the Ganga river after five years of the project;
(c) the existing data for TDS and pH levels for the Ganga river water for major cities along the river like Haridwar, Kanpur, Allahabad, Varanasi and Patna, whether the water is potable if consumed from the river; and
(d) the details of chemicals found in Ganga water along cities?

J

(a) the number of deaths and injuries involving railway personnel, including regular employees, contractural workers and outsourced workforce, during construction, maintenance, inspection or coupling of trains in the last three years, zone-wise details;
(b) the details of the compensation provided to such workers’ families, category-wise, zone-wise;
(c) the details of the installation of the RAKSHAK system, zone-wise and details of track percentage covered by the RAKSHAK system and the amount spent for installation, training and operationalisation; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure safety of workers and social security measures available to different category of workers in case of injury or death?

(a) the number of Indian workers in Israel across occupation, including the number of Indian workers sent to Israel after the beginning of Israel-Hamas conflict on 7 October, 2023;
(b) whether Indian workers in Israel have protection of labour rights through the Central Government;
(c) the number and details of Indian citizens killed or injured in Israel-Palestine since 7 October, 2023, including details of perpetrators and the action taken by the Central Government against them; and
(d) whether the Central Government has provided any compensation to the families of those killed or injured?

(a) the procedure followed by the National Testing Agency (NTA) to award contracts for conducting examinations through private vendors;
(b) list of vendors and amounts paid State-wise;
(c) the number of complaints received against such vendors during the conduct of various examination and  the action taken by NTA since its inception; and
(d) the status of enquiry of 2024 NEET Examination paper leak and details of the action taken against those found guilty of malpractices?

(a) the plan that Government and the Airport Authority of India (AAI) has made for the holistic development of the Kozhikode Airport to enable the airport to operate with large-bodied aircrafts;
(b) the progress being made in expanding the runway after the State Government acquired land for the purpose;
(c) whether Government is aware that the Kozhikode airport is operating without a full-time Director since August, 2024 which is hampering the everyday operations and development activities at the airport; and 
(d) the steps Government and the AAI has taken to appoint a full-time Director?

(a) the number of domestic flights cancelled during the last three years, including reasons for cancellations as provided by the respective airlines;
(b) the yearly number of passengers affected by such cancellations and details of the compensation provided to the passengers, if any, airline-wise;
(c) whether Government and the DGCA have taken note of frequent cancellations and delays causing inconvenience to passengers, if so, the details of the action taken against airlines and officials; and
(d) whether the DGCA will formulate any Standard-Operating-Procedure (SOP) in cases of cancellations and inordinate delays to help the passengers?
